DESCRIPTION:April Fools' Day falls on April 1 and is kept across much of th
 e Western world with no agreed account of where it came from. Asked the or
 igin question directly\, a Library of Congress folklorist answered: "The s
 hort answer is that nobody knows for sure." The uncertainty is not a moder
 n failing — an almanac verse printed in 1760 already conceded that the p
 eople keeping the day could not say why.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/ho
 liday/april-fools-day/
